          </div>
          <div class="side">
            <p class="lede" set:html={hero.ledeHtml} />
            <div class="cta">
              <a class="btn" href="#explore">Letâ€™s explore <span class="arr">â†’</span></a>
              <a class="ghost" href="#work">How we work</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ SKETCH SCENE â€” big unboxed sketch, two text beats, ambient gradient ============ -->
    <section class="sk" id="look" data-sketch>
      <div class="pin">
        <div class="ambient" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="gb g1"></span><span class="gb g2"></span><span class="gb g3"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="grid">
            <div class="txt">
              <div class="fill"><i data-fill></i></div>
              <div class="beat b1" data-beat1>
                <h2>Sometimes, you already know enough. Yet thereâ€™s still <em>a missing piece.</em></h2>
                <p>Something you canâ€™t quite put your finger on.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="beat b2" data-beat2>
                <h2>It could be a conversation. A different perspective. <em>A small decision.</em></h2>
                <p>Or simply seeing something you thought you knew in a different way.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="art">
              <img src={look.sketch.src} alt={look.sketch.alt} data-img1 />
              <img src={shift.row.sketch.src} alt={shift.row.sketch.alt} data-img2 />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ MAKE THE SHIFT â€” grey card, black text + circular growing period ============ -->
    <section class="shiftcard" data-shiftcard>
      <div class="pin">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Where the shift begins</span>
          <h2 class="line"><span class="w">Make</span> <span class="w">the</span> <span class="w serif">shift</span><span class="period"><span class="pdot"></span></span></h2>
          <p class="sub">Maybe it starts with a better question. Or a clearer observation. Perhaps you see a possibility you hadnâ€™t considered â€” <span class="serif">and thatâ€™s where the shift begins.</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="wipe" data-wipe aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ MAKE THE SHIFT (horizontal; bg blackâ†’grey when "A possibility" centres) ============ -->
    <section class="mts" data-mts>
      <div class="pin">
        <div class="ghost" data-ghost>
          <b class="w">A thought</b>
          <span class="arw"><em>becomes</em><i aria-hidden="true">â†’</i></span>
          <b class="w" data-poss>A possibility</b>
          <span class="arw"><em>becomes</em><i aria-hidden="true">â†’</i></span>
          <b class="w">A decision</b>
          <span class="arw"><em>becomes</em><i aria-hidden="true">â†’</i></span>
          <b class="w">Action</b>
        </div>
        <div class="fg">
          <p class="intro" data-mts-intro>Not everything needs a new plan. Sometimes, it needs <span class="serif">a new way of looking</span> at the old one.</p>
          <p class="outro" data-mts-outro>Small shifts can change <span class="serif">what happens next.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ ABOUT / MANIFESTO â€” warm gradient card (no circles) ============ -->
    <section class="aboutcard">
